# Domain Layer

Innermost layer of the Onion. Pure Python — no framework, no database,
no ORM imports.

Rules:
- Every entity is a plain class (`__init__` + optional `__eq__`).
- Repository interfaces are abstract (`abc.ABC`) — define the contract,
  never the implementation.
- Domain services contain business logic that spans multiple entities
  or doesn't naturally belong to a single entity.
- Domain NEVER imports from `application/` or `infrastructure/`.
- `application/` may import from domain.
- `infrastructure/` may import from both domain and application.

Files per bounded context:
- `entity.py` — the domain entity
- `repository.py` — abstract repository port (interface)
- `service.py` — domain service (pure business logic)
